  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The compound(s) which react with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;to form Boron nitride <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>BN</mi></mfenced></math> is/are:</p><p>(A) Amorphous <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><munder><mo>&#10230;</mo><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Tempreature</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow></munder><mi>BN</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p>(B) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><munder><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mfenced><mi>excess</mi></mfenced></munder><mover><mo>&#10230;</mo><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>HighTemp</mi><mo>.&#160;</mo></mrow></mover><msub><mfenced><mi>BN</mi></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></msub></math></p><p>(C) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mover><mo>&#10230;</mo><mrow><mn>900</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow></mover><mn>2</mn><mi>BN</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math></p><p>(D) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>HBF</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#10230;</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><msubsup><mi>NH</mi><mn>4</mn><mo>&#8853;</mo></msubsup></mfenced><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><msubsup><mi>BF</mi><mn>4</mn><mo>&#8854;</mo></msubsup></mfenced></math></p><p>Hence, (A,B,C)&nbsp;are correct</p>",
    "image": null
